  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="66d7-13b6-bd00-5988" name="Assyrian Empire (Armies of Antiquity) - List Notes" publicationId="aab0-aa1e-0319-4ffe" hidden="false">
      <description>ASSYRIAN EMPIRE ARMY LIST (Armies of Antiquity, pp.10-11), from the reforms of Tiglath Pileser III to the fall of Nineveh.
Characters: the army may have a General and an Army Standard Bearer. Chariotry &amp; Cavalry up to half the points; Infantry at least a quarter; Auxiliaries up to half; Allies &amp; Mercenaries up to a quarter.
Special rules: Terrifying Reputation (fear in enemy units with Ld 7 or less until an Assyrian chariot, cavalry or infantry unit breaks) and Highly Professional (the Assyrians choose who moves first if it would be random).

ARMY COMPOSITION (percentages by points):
  Chariotry &amp; Cavalry: up to 50%
  Infantry: at least 25%
  Auxiliaries: up to 50%
  Allies &amp; Mercenaries: up to 25%</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
